Advantages:
Cost Efficiency: Reduced complexity in manufacturing and supply chain management can lead to significant cost savings.

Ease of Maintenance and Repair: Standardized components simplify maintenance and repair processes, as the same parts can be used across different products.

Sustainability: By reducing the variety of components produced, standardization can lead to less waste and more efficient use of resources.

Scalability: Standardized designs allow for scalability in production. As demand increases, it's easier to ramp up production without significant changes to the manufacturing process.

Challenges:
Innovation Constraints: Overemphasis on standardization might limit innovation, as designers might be restricted to using standard components.
Market Differentiation: Differentiating products in the market can be challenging if they are made up of standardized components.